  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$An explanation that holds up only because nobody has checked it is not worth ______.$qb$, $qb$trusting$qb$, $qb$repeating$qb$, $qb$recording$qb$, $qb$shortening$qb$, $qb$approving$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Telling a customer what a product cannot do protects the sale that comes ______.$qb$, $qb$after$qb$, $qb$first$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, $qb$quickly$qb$, $qb$instead$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A figure changed to make a report look better is no longer a ______.$qb$, $qb$measurement$qb$, $qb$report$qb$, $qb$target$qb$, $qb$headline$qb$, $qb$summary$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A gift from a supplier is paid for the next time you have to choose between ______.$qb$, $qb$suppliers$qb$, $qb$meetings$qb$, $qb$invoices$qb$, $qb$branches$qb$, $qb$colleagues$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Staying silent about something you saw makes you part of what happens ______.$qb$, $qb$next$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$quietly$qb$, $qb$publicly$qb$, $qb$instead$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A shortcut that works because nobody is watching is a ______, not a method.$qb$, $qb$risk$qb$, $qb$saving$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$preference$qb$, $qb$schedule$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Being trusted takes years and is spent in a single ______.$qb$, $qb$moment$qb$, $qb$invoice$qb$, $qb$target$qb$, $qb$roster$qb$, $qb$schedule$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The time to raise a concern is while the decision can still be ______.$qb$, $qb$changed$qb$, $qb$explained$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$understood$qb$, $qb$published$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A conflict of interest is easier to manage once it has been ______.$qb$, $qb$declared$qb$, $qb$printed$qb$, $qb$measured$qb$, $qb$approved$qb$, $qb$avoided$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Work presented as your own when it was not is a debt that stays ______.$qb$, $qb$unpaid$qb$, $qb$hidden$qb$, $qb$small$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have found a mistake in your own work that nobody else has noticed. It would take a day to correct. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Report it and say what correcting it would involve$qb$, $qb$Correct it and mention it afterwards$qb$, $qb$Work out how much difference it makes before deciding$qb$, $qb$Correct it quietly, since the outcome is the same$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since nobody has noticed it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer has been undercharged by a significant amount and has already paid. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager so the customer can be contacted$qb$, $qb$Contact the customer and explain the error$qb$, $qb$Correct the price on the account for next time$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether the customer notices$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the error was the company's$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A supplier offers you tickets to an event. You are involved in choosing suppliers. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Decline and tell your manager the offer was made$qb$, $qb$Decline the offer politely$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager whether you may accept them$qb$, $qb$Accept them and mention it if it becomes relevant$qb$, $qb$Accept them, since a gift will not change your judgement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to sign a document confirming checks you did not carry out. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Say what you did check and sign only for that$qb$, $qb$Refuse to sign until the checks are done$qb$, $qb$Ask who is meant to have done the checks$qb$, $qb$Sign it and carry out the checks afterwards$qb$, $qb$Sign it, since the checks are usually a formality$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague asks you to say he was in the office when he was not. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Tell him you will not, and why$qb$, $qb$Tell him he will need to ask someone else$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he needs you to say it$qb$, $qb$Agree, since it is a small thing between colleagues$qb$, $qb$Say nothing either way and hope it is not raised$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your company's advertising claims something about a product that you know is not accurate. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with whoever is responsible for the claim$qb$, $qb$Check whether the claim is actually inaccurate$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your own manager$qb$, $qb$Avoid repeating the claim to customers yourself$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since advertising is not your area$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are collecting feedback and one response is strongly negative. Including it will make the overall result look worse. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Include it and report the result as it stands$qb$, $qb$Include it and note that one response was an outlier$qb$, $qb$Report the result both with and without it$qb$, $qb$Exclude it and mention that one response was excluded$qb$, $qb$Exclude it, since one response is not representative$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer asks whether your product will do something. It will do most of it but not all. What is the best answer?$qb$, $qb$Say what it will and will not do$qb$, $qb$Say yes, and mention the limitations afterwards$qb$, $qb$Ask what he needs it for before answering$qb$, $qb$Say yes, since it does most of what he wants$qb$, $qb$Say yes and deal with any problem afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been given access to information you should not be able to see. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Report the access problem and stop using it$qb$, $qb$Stop using it and say nothing further$qb$, $qb$Ask whether you were meant to have the access$qb$, $qb$Use it only for the work you need it for$qb$, $qb$Use it, since it was given to you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague has made a claim in a meeting that you know is untrue. It relates to her own work and others are acting on it. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Raise the point in the meeting so the record is corrected$qb$, $qb$Speak to her afterwards and ask her to correct it$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your manager after the meeting$qb$, $qb$Ask a question that gives her a chance to correct it$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since it is her work and not yours$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have made a promise to a customer that you now realise you cannot keep. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Tell him now and say what you can do instead$qb$, $qb$Tell him now that the promise cannot be kept$qb$, $qb$Work out whether anyone else could deliver it$qb$, $qb$Wait until the deadline and explain then$qb$, $qb$Deliver what you can and hope it is enough$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager asks you to leave something out of a report because it makes the team look bad. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Explain why it needs to be in and ask her to reconsider$qb$, $qb$Ask her what specifically concerns her about including it$qb$, $qb$Include it in a way that draws less attention$qb$, $qb$Leave it out and mention it to her separately$qb$, $qb$Leave it out, since she is responsible for the report$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You realise a policy your team follows is unfair to one group of customers. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with whoever can change the policy$qb$, $qb$Check whether the unfairness is what you think it is$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your own manager$qb$, $qb$Apply the policy less strictly to that group$qb$, $qb$Follow the policy, since it is not yours to change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked for a reference for a former colleague whose work was poor. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Give an accurate account of the work you saw$qb$, $qb$Confirm the dates and role and nothing further$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the reference is required to be detailed$qb$, $qb$Give a positive reference, since he needs the job$qb$, $qb$Decline to give a reference at all$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You discover a colleague has been rounding figures in a way that always favours the team's results. What is the best first step?$qb$, $qb$Ask her how the rounding is being done$qb$, $qb$Report it to your manager$qb$, $qb$Check the figures yourself first$qb$, $qb$Tell her it needs to stop$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since rounding is a small thing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer complaint is partly justified and partly not. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Accept the part that is justified and explain the rest$qb$, $qb$Accept the complaint and put the whole thing right$qb$, $qb$Explain which parts you accept and which you do not$qb$, $qb$Apologise generally without going into which parts$qb$, $qb$Reject the complaint, since it is not fully accurate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are competing with a colleague for a promotion and learn something that would damage his chances. It is true but unrelated to the role. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Nothing, since it has no bearing on the role$qb$, $qb$Tell your colleague you heard it, so he knows it is circulating$qb$, $qb$Raise it only if you are asked directly$qb$, $qb$Mention it to your manager without saying who told you$qb$, $qb$Raise it, since the decision should use all the facts$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team has hit its target only because of a change in how something is counted. You are asked to report the result. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Report the result and explain the counting change$qb$, $qb$Report the result as it has been calculated$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the counting change was intended$qb$, $qb$Report the result and mention the change if asked$qb$, $qb$Report the result, since the target was formally met$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A friend asks you for information about your employer that is not public. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Say you are not able to share it$qb$, $qb$Say you would rather not discuss work$qb$, $qb$Ask why she wants to know before answering$qb$, $qb$Share the part that seems harmless$qb$, $qb$Share it, since she will not pass it on$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been praised for work that was mostly done by someone who has since left. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Say who did the work$qb$, $qb$Accept the praise and mention her contribution$qb$, $qb$Say that it was a joint effort$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since she is no longer here to mind$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since correcting it would be awkward$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a pharmacy. You have just realised you gave a customer the wrong strength of a medicine an hour ago. It is not dangerous but it is wrong. He has left with it. How do you handle this?$qb$, $qb$Tell the pharmacist now and contact the customer straight away$qb$, $qb$Contact the customer straight away and put it right$qb$, $qb$Tell the pharmacist and ask how she wants it handled$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether the customer returns or calls$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the wrong strength will not harm him$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a mechanic. You have finished a service and realise you forgot to check the brakes, which is part of the service. The customer is at the counter paying. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell her now, do the check, and delay her by the time it takes$qb$, $qb$Tell her the check was missed and ask her to bring it back$qb$, $qb$Do the check quickly before she leaves without telling her$qb$, $qb$Sign it off, since the brakes felt fine when you drove it$qb$, $qb$Sign it off and check them next time she comes in$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a junior member of an accounts team. You have noticed that a senior colleague regularly approves his own expenses, which the rules do not allow. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your manager, describing what you have seen$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the senior colleague directly$qb$, $qb$Check the rules carefully before raising it with anyone$qb$, $qb$Mention it to a colleague to see whether they have noticed$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since he is senior and it is not your area$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a shop. A customer has returned an item claiming it was faulty. You can see the damage was caused by misuse. The refund would come from your branch's figures. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show her what you can see and explain the position$qb$, $qb$Explain that the damage does not look like a fault$qb$, $qb$Refer it to your manager to decide$qb$, $qb$Give the refund to avoid an argument at the counter$qb$, $qb$Refuse the refund without explaining your reasoning$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a site supervisor. A contractor has done work that meets the specification but you know a cheaper material was used than the one quoted. The client has not noticed. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the client what was used and what it means for them$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the contractor and ask for an explanation$qb$, $qb$Check whether the substitution was formally agreed$qb$, $qb$Note it and mention it if the client ever asks$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the work meets the specification$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher. A parent has offered you a substantial gift at the end of term. Your school has no written policy on gifts. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Decline it and tell your head teacher it was offered$qb$, $qb$Decline it politely and explain why$qb$, $qb$Ask your head teacher whether you may accept it$qb$, $qb$Accept it and mention it to your head teacher afterwards$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since there is no policy against it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a call centre. Your team's figures are measured on call length. A colleague has told you that ending calls early and letting customers ring back improves the figures. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell your team leader that the figures are being worked around$qb$, $qb$Tell your colleague you will not do that$qb$, $qb$Ask your colleague how widespread the practice is$qb$, $qb$Carry on as you are and say nothing about it$qb$, $qb$Do the same, since everyone is measured the same way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ETH-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a delivery driver. You have damaged a customer's gatepost while reversing. Nobody saw it and the damage is small. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer now and report it to your depot$qb$, $qb$Leave a note with your details and report it$qb$, $qb$Report it to your depot and let them contact the customer$qb$, $qb$Mention it only if the customer contacts the company$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the damage is small and nobody saw$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
