  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have figures from two branches collected by different methods. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Compare each branch against its own past figures$qb$, $qb$Adjust one set of figures to match the other$qb$, $qb$Compare them and note the difference in method$qb$, $qb$Recollect both sets using one method$qb$, $qb$Use the branch with the more reliable method$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A measure has hit its target every month for two years. What is worth considering?$qb$, $qb$Whether the target sits below what would happen anyway$qb$, $qb$How honestly the measure is being recorded$qb$, $qb$Raising the target to something harder to reach$qb$, $qb$The possibility that the process is unusually stable$qb$, $qb$Dropping a measure that never varies$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably tells you whether a change has made a difference?$qb$, $qb$Comparing with something that did not change$qb$, $qb$Measuring before and after the change$qb$, $qb$Asking the people affected by it$qb$, $qb$Watching the measure for long enough$qb$, $qb$Checking whether the change was applied properly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer survey had a nine per cent response rate. What can you conclude?$qb$, $qb$It describes the nine per cent who answered$qb$, $qb$The results are not usable$qb$, $qb$The results may still be broadly right$qb$, $qb$More responses are needed before using it$qb$, $qb$The survey was badly designed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to report a figure you know is measured inconsistently. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Report it with a note on how it is measured$qb$, $qb$Report it as it stands$qb$, $qb$Fix the measurement before reporting$qb$, $qb$Report a range instead of a single figure$qb$, $qb$Decline to report it until it is reliable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
