  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a milk collection society. One village's milk consistently tests lower in fat than the others. The farmers there insist their cattle are the same breed and feed. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Look at when and how the samples from that village are taken$qb$, $qb$Test a fresh sample from several farmers there yourself$qb$, $qb$Ask the collection agent about that village's routine$qb$, $qb$Retest the village's milk at a different laboratory$qb$, $qb$Pay that village at the lower rate the tests indicate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
