  ($qb$HEAIL-DLE-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a school attendance office. One class shows attendance of ninety-eight per cent while teachers report a third of pupils regularly absent. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Watch how the register is taken in that class$qb$, $qb$Compare the register with the teachers' own records$qb$, $qb$Ask the class teacher about the register$qb$, $qb$Retake the register yourself for a week$qb$, $qb$Report the ninety-eight per cent as recorded$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
