  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably reduces bias in a hiring decision?$qb$, $qb$Asking every candidate the same questions in the same order$qb$, $qb$Having more than one person on the panel$qb$, $qb$Reminding the panel to be objective$qb$, $qb$Recording the reasons for the decision$qb$, $qb$Removing names from applications$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone on your team has asked for a change to their working hours for a health reason. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what they need the change to achieve$qb$, $qb$Ask what hours they would like to work$qb$, $qb$Check whether the change is allowed by policy$qb$, $qb$Ask whether others would want the same$qb$, $qb$Agree to the change they have requested$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member's ideas are regularly repeated by someone else and credited to them. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Name the original source at the time it happens$qb$, $qb$Speak to the person who repeated it afterwards$qb$, $qb$Tell the original person you noticed$qb$, $qb$Raise how ideas are credited with the whole team$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the idea reached the group either way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your recruitment has produced very similar people for three years. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Look at where the applications are coming from$qb$, $qb$Change the questions asked at interview$qb$, $qb$Widen where the role is advertised$qb$, $qb$Add someone different to the interview panel$qb$, $qb$Set a target for a more varied intake$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
