  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are chairing a meeting and one person has not spoken in forty minutes. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask them directly for their view on the current point$qb$, $qb$Invite anyone who has not spoken to contribute$qb$, $qb$Speak to them after the meeting$qb$, $qb$Continue, since they can speak if they wish$qb$, $qb$Ask them to prepare something for next time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A job advertisement lists ten requirements, four of which are not really needed. What is the main effect?$qb$, $qb$People who could do the job do not apply$qb$, $qb$The advertisement takes longer to read$qb$, $qb$Unsuitable candidates apply anyway$qb$, $qb$The requirements look more impressive$qb$, $qb$The advertisement costs more to place$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
