  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage an e-waste dismantling unit. A worker with a hearing impairment has asked to move away from the crushing bay where he cannot hear warnings. There is a quieter bench available. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Move him and check what else in the unit depends on hearing warnings$qb$, $qb$Move him to the quieter bench as he has asked$qb$, $qb$Ask him what other difficulties he has in the unit$qb$, $qb$Check whether the policy allows the move$qb$, $qb$Ask him to work with someone who can alert him$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INC-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a drone survey firm. Two surveyors are equally qualified but you always send the same one to client sites because clients seem to respond better to him. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Send the other and find out whether the client difference is real$qb$, $qb$Alternate between the two surveyors from now on$qb$, $qb$Ask clients what they value in a site surveyor$qb$, $qb$Send the second surveyor with the first a few times$qb$, $qb$Continue, since client response affects the business$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
