  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to say when someone challenges your work in a meeting?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they would do differently$qb$, $qb$Explain the reasoning behind your approach$qb$, $qb$Say you will look at their point afterwards$qb$, $qb$Ask them to put the challenge in writing$qb$, $qb$Defend the parts you are confident about$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your idea was rejected in favour of a colleague's. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Help make his idea work as well as it can$qb$, $qb$Support the decision without further comment$qb$, $qb$Ask why his idea was preferred$qb$, $qb$Offer your idea again if his runs into trouble$qb$, $qb$Say nothing and see how his idea performs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A mistake was made by your team and you were not involved in it. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Answer for it as the team's, then sort it internally$qb$, $qb$Explain who was responsible and what is being done$qb$, $qb$Say the team made the mistake without naming anyone$qb$, $qb$Say you were not involved but will help fix it$qb$, $qb$Let the person responsible answer for it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to judge whether a colleague takes correction well. What would tell you?$qb$, $qb$They ask questions rather than explain themselves$qb$, $qb$They accept the correction without argument$qb$, $qb$They change what they do afterwards$qb$, $qb$They thank the person who corrected them$qb$, $qb$They do not repeat the mistake$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are the most experienced person present and a newer colleague suggests a better method. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Use hers and say where yours fell short$qb$, $qb$Try both and let the comparison settle it$qb$, $qb$Use hers and thank her for the suggestion$qb$, $qb$Explain why yours has worked until now$qb$, $qb$Use hers without comment on the difference$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer has complained about something you did. What is the most useful first step?$qb$, $qb$Find out what the customer experienced$qb$, $qb$Explain what actually happened from your side$qb$, $qb$Apologise and offer to put it right$qb$, $qb$Check the records before responding$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague what they would do$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
