  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager takes credit for your work in front of others. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with him privately afterwards$qb$, $qb$Mention your part factually at the time$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether they noticed it too$qb$, $qb$Let it go and make your work visible another way$qb$, $qb$Take it above him to his own manager$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually makes it hard for someone to admit an error?$qb$, $qb$They believe it reflects on their competence$qb$, $qb$They fear the consequences of admitting it$qb$, $qb$They are not certain it was their error$qb$, $qb$They do not want to let the team down$qb$, $qb$They think it can be quietly corrected$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been asked to review work by someone senior to you and it has a flaw. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Raise the flaw as you would with anyone$qb$, $qb$Raise it privately rather than in the review$qb$, $qb$Ask a question that lets him find it$qb$, $qb$Mention it as something you may have misread$qb$, $qb$Note it and see whether anyone else raises it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a stage lighting hire company. A rig you specified was wrong for the venue and the event ran with poor lighting. The client is on the phone asking what happened. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say the specification was mine and it was wrong, then set out the fix$qb$, $qb$Say the rig did not suit the venue and offer a replacement$qb$, $qb$Explain what information the specification was based on$qb$, $qb$Say the venue details you were given were incomplete$qb$, $qb$Offer a discount and move the conversation to the next event$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
