  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a calligraphy studio. A client praised a piece to you that was mostly done by your assistant while you were away. The client believes you did it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell the client who did it and let the credit go there$qb$, $qb$Say your assistant did most of the work on it$qb$, $qb$Thank the client and tell your assistant afterwards$qb$, $qb$Say it was a joint piece from the studio$qb$, $qb$Accept the praise, since the studio's name is on it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a model-making shop. A method you introduced two years ago is now slowing the work, and a junior has proposed replacing it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Try his method and say plainly if it beats the current one$qb$, $qb$Ask him to explain how his method would work$qb$, $qb$Trial both methods and compare the output$qb$, $qb$Explain why the current method was introduced$qb$, $qb$Ask the team which method they would prefer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a cargo weighing office. A dispute with a haulier has gone on for a week and you have just found the error was in your own records. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the haulier the error was ours and settle it today$qb$, $qb$Correct the records and inform the haulier$qb$, $qb$Explain how the error came to be made$qb$, $qb$Settle the dispute without saying where the error was$qb$, $qb$Correct it quietly and let the dispute lapse$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a seed drying yard. A batch was spoiled because you overruled the yard foreman on drying time. He has said nothing about it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say in front of the team that the call was mine and wrong$qb$, $qb$Tell the foreman privately that he was right$qb$, $qb$Record the loss and change the drying instruction$qb$, $qb$Say the batch was spoiled without going into the decision$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the foreman has not raised it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a puppet theatre. A reviewer has praised a scene that your co-director designed and attributed it to you by name. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Correct the record publicly and name her$qb$, $qb$Tell the reviewer privately who designed it$qb$, $qb$Tell your co-director that you have seen the review$qb$, $qb$Mention her contribution the next time you are asked$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the theatre benefits either way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a kite festival office. You insisted on a launch site that turned out to be badly chosen, and the day went poorly. The committee is meeting tomorrow. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Open by saying the site was my choice and what I misjudged$qb$, $qb$Present what went wrong and what should change next year$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether the site is raised before speaking$qb$, $qb$Explain the reasons the site looked suitable$qb$, $qb$Note the weather conditions that affected the day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a rope-making works. A long-standing customer has complained about quality, and you know the change came from a cheaper fibre you chose. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell him I changed the fibre and what I will do about it$qb$, $qb$Ask him to describe the quality difference he is seeing$qb$, $qb$Change back to the old fibre without explaining why$qb$, $qb$Explain the cost pressure that led to the change$qb$, $qb$Offer a price reduction without discussing the fibre$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise an incense stick drying floor. Output has fallen since you rearranged the racks, though nobody has connected the two. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say the rearrangement was mine and put the racks back$qb$, $qb$Put the racks back and see whether output recovers$qb$, $qb$Ask the floor workers what has changed for them$qb$, $qb$Compare output before and after the rearrangement$qb$, $qb$Wait, since the fall may have another cause$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
