  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a cheese ripening room. You argued against installing humidity monitors and a batch has spoiled that monitors would have caught. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say I was wrong about the monitors and ask for them now$qb$, $qb$Request the monitors on the basis of the spoiled batch$qb$, $qb$Report the loss and its likely cause$qb$, $qb$Note that the batch may have spoiled anyway$qb$, $qb$Ask for monitors without revisiting your earlier view$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-EGO-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bell-casting foundry office. A casting failed and the moulder, the metallurgist and you each made a contributing decision. The owner wants an explanation. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set out all three decisions including mine, then the fix$qb$, $qb$Explain the sequence of decisions without attributing them$qb$, $qb$Describe your own decision and let the others describe theirs$qb$, $qb$Say the failure had several causes across the team$qb$, $qb$Explain the two decisions that mattered most$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
