  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A workplace where nobody thanks anyone is not unkind, only ______.$qb$, $qb$inattentive$qb$, $qb$efficient$qb$, $qb$formal$qb$, $qb$understaffed$qb$, $qb$punctual$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Hope that rests on nothing collapses at the first piece of ______.$qb$, $qb$evidence$qb$, $qb$praise$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$advice$qb$, $qb$funding$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who has just had bad news needs the news acknowledged before the ______.$qb$, $qb$encouragement$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$decision$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$handover$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your organisation has announced job cuts and your team is anxious. What is most useful to say?$qb$, $qb$What is known, what is not, and when you will know more$qb$, $qb$That you will support them through whatever happens$qb$, $qb$That the cuts may not affect your team$qb$, $qb$That worrying now will not change the outcome$qb$, $qb$That you are as concerned as they are$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague has worked hard on something that was then cancelled. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what her work showed that will still be used$qb$, $qb$Thank her for the effort she put in$qb$, $qb$Tell her the cancellation was nothing to do with her work$qb$, $qb$Suggest she puts it forward again another time$qb$, $qb$Say that cancellations are part of the job$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably keeps a team going through a difficult period?$qb$, $qb$Being told honestly what is happening and when$qb$, $qb$Being reassured that things will improve$qb$, $qb$Being praised for coping with the difficulty$qb$, $qb$Being kept busy so there is less time to worry$qb$, $qb$Being told others have it worse$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone tells you their work is going badly. What is the most useful first response?$qb$, $qb$Ask what part is going badly$qb$, $qb$Say that you have had periods like that too$qb$, $qb$Point out what they have done well recently$qb$, $qb$Offer to help with the difficult part$qb$, $qb$Tell them it will improve with time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member does something small and useful that nobody notices. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what you saw and why it mattered$qb$, $qb$Thank them for what they did$qb$, $qb$Mention it at the next team meeting$qb$, $qb$Note it for their next review$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since it was a small thing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main problem with telling a struggling team that everything will be fine?$qb$, $qb$They stop believing what you tell them$qb$, $qb$It does not address what they are worried about$qb$, $qb$It may turn out not to be true$qb$, $qb$It sounds as though you are not listening$qb$, $qb$It gives them nothing to do$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A change has gone badly and your team is discouraged. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Name one thing that worked and build the next step on it$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge that the change has gone badly$qb$, $qb$Explain what will be different next time$qb$, $qb$Ask the team what they think should happen$qb$, $qb$Move quickly to the next piece of work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when only problems get discussed in team meetings?$qb$, $qb$The team stops seeing what is working$qb$, $qb$Meetings become unpleasant to attend$qb$, $qb$People bring fewer problems forward$qb$, $qb$The team focuses on the wrong things$qb$, $qb$Morale falls over time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague is going through something difficult outside work. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make this period easier here$qb$, $qb$Tell them to let you know if they need anything$qb$, $qb$Reduce their workload without discussing it$qb$, $qb$Give them space and avoid raising it$qb$, $qb$Tell them you are sorry to hear about it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone thanks you for work you found straightforward. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Accept it and say what part was worth doing$qb$, $qb$Accept the thanks simply$qb$, $qb$Say that it was no trouble at all$qb$, $qb$Explain that it was easier than it looked$qb$, $qb$Say that anyone would have done the same$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team has missed a target for the third time. How should the discussion start?$qb$, $qb$What has got closer since the first attempt$qb$, $qb$What went wrong this time$qb$, $qb$What the target means for the business$qb$, $qb$What you expect to be different next time$qb$, $qb$How disappointing the result is$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What makes an expression of thanks land rather than sound routine?$qb$, $qb$It names something only that person could have done$qb$, $qb$The gap between the work and the thanks is short$qb$, $qb$Other people are present when it is said$qb$, $qb$Someone senior is the one saying it$qb$, $qb$There is a written record of it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A member of your team has been holding the group together informally and nobody has said so. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say to the team what he has been doing$qb$, $qb$Thank him privately for what he does$qb$, $qb$Give him a formal role that reflects it$qb$, $qb$Mention it in his next review$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since he may not want attention$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is most useful when a team is asked to do more with less?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly what will not get done$qb$, $qb$Ask the team how to absorb the extra$qb$, $qb$Encourage the team to find efficiencies$qb$, $qb$Thank the team for taking it on$qb$, $qb$Explain why the reduction was necessary$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has helped you at real cost to their own work. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell their manager what they did for you$qb$, $qb$Thank them and offer to return the favour$qb$, $qb$Thank them at the time and again afterwards$qb$, $qb$Make sure they are not left short as a result$qb$, $qb$Thank them and mention it to the team$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens to a team told only that they must stay positive?$qb$, $qb$Real concerns stop being voiced$qb$, $qb$The team pretends to be more positive$qb$, $qb$Morale falls further than before$qb$, $qb$People become frustrated with the message$qb$, $qb$The instruction is quietly ignored$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team has absorbed extra work for the third month running. What is most useful to say to them?$qb$, $qb$What you have taken off them, or that you have not managed to$qb$, $qb$That you know it is a lot and have raised it upward$qb$, $qb$That the extra work should ease next month$qb$, $qb$That you appreciate the effort they are putting in$qb$, $qb$That every team is under the same pressure$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
