  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone in your team is consistently negative in meetings. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would need to change for it to be worth trying$qb$, $qb$Ask them to raise concerns with a suggestion attached$qb$, $qb$Speak to them about the effect on the team$qb$, $qb$Ask others whether they share the view$qb$, $qb$Let it pass, since the concerns may be valid$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-036$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a hand-pump repair crew. The monsoon has flooded three sites and the week's work has been undone twice. The crew are wet, tired and saying there is no point going back out. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say what the week has actually fixed, then agree what today can realistically finish$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge that the week has been wasted and thank them for staying$qb$, $qb$Tell them the flooding will pass and the work will hold next time$qb$, $qb$Send them home and restart when conditions improve$qb$, $qb$Remind them that the villages depend on the pumps working$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a bamboo scaffolding yard. A large contract has been cancelled and the yard will be quiet for two months. Your team of nine has heard the news. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell them what work is confirmed, what is not, and when you will know more$qb$, $qb$Tell them the contract is cancelled and that you are looking for more work$qb$, $qb$Reassure them that quiet periods have happened before$qb$, $qb$Say nothing until you know whether jobs are at risk$qb$, $qb$Ask them to suggest how the two months could be used$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a terracotta tile works. A kiln firing failed and a fortnight of work was lost. The team who loaded it are blaming themselves. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say what the loading did correctly, then look at the firing itself$qb$, $qb$Tell them the loss is not their fault$qb$, $qb$Find out what caused the firing to fail$qb$, $qb$Tell them these losses happen in this trade$qb$, $qb$Ask them to load the next kiln more carefully$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a khadi weaving centre. A weaver has spent three weeks on a piece for an order that has since been withdrawn. She is upset. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show her where the piece can still be sold and price it properly$qb$, $qb$Tell her the piece is good work regardless of the order$qb$, $qb$Explain that the withdrawal had nothing to do with her$qb$, $qb$Offer her the next order to make up the time$qb$, $qb$Tell her that withdrawn orders are part of the trade$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a block-ice delivery round. A driver has covered another's route for a fortnight on top of his own, without being asked and without mentioning it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell the depot what he covered and make sure he is not left short$qb$, $qb$Thank him for covering the extra route$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he did not mention it$qb$, $qb$Note it for his next pay review$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since he chose to do it himself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a sericulture rearing house. A disease has killed most of a rearing and the team has to start again. Two rearers have said they are thinking of leaving. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make the next rearing worth staying for$qb$, $qb$Tell them the disease was outside anyone's control$qb$, $qb$Explain what will be done differently next rearing$qb$, $qb$Ask them to give it one more rearing before deciding$qb$, $qb$Tell them losses like this happen every few years$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a betel leaf packing unit. Work is repetitive and the packers rarely hear anything except when a consignment is rejected. How do you change this?$qb$, $qb$Tell them which consignments went through clean and what that took$qb$, $qb$Thank the packers for their work at the end of each week$qb$, $qb$Explain why rejected consignments have to be raised$qb$, $qb$Introduce a bonus for consignments with no rejections$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since rejections are the thing that needs attention$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a tamarind processing unit. Prices have fallen and you have had to cut overtime. The team has taken the news badly. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say how long the cut is expected to last and what would end it$qb$, $qb$Explain why the overtime had to be cut$qb$, $qb$Tell them you will restore it as soon as you can$qb$, $qb$Thank them for accepting the reduction$qb$, $qb$Ask them to be patient until prices recover$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a copra drying yard. A worker who has been here twenty years is retiring next month and nobody has mentioned it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say to the yard what he has done here over twenty years$qb$, $qb$Arrange something to mark his last day$qb$, $qb$Thank him privately before he leaves$qb$, $qb$Ask the team what they would like to do$qb$, $qb$Follow whatever the usual practice is for retirements$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a lac bangle unit. Sales have been poor for three months and the artisans have begun talking about it constantly during work. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell them what you know about the market and what you are trying$qb$, $qb$Ask them what they think is causing the fall$qb$, $qb$Reassure them that sales will recover$qb$, $qb$Ask them to keep the talk out of working hours$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the talk will pass$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a palm jaggery boiling shed. The boiler has been repaired three times this season and the crew have stopped expecting it to hold. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say what the repairs have and have not fixed, and what happens next$qb$, $qb$Tell them the next repair should be the last$qb$, $qb$Ask them what they notice before it fails$qb$, $qb$Thank them for working around the breakdowns$qb$, $qb$Tell them a new boiler is not affordable this season$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a coir rope twisting unit. A worker regularly helps newer staff at the cost of her own output, and her figures look worse because of it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say to the unit what she has been doing and count it properly$qb$, $qb$Thank her for helping the newer staff$qb$, $qb$Adjust how her output is measured$qb$, $qb$Give her a formal role training new starters$qb$, $qb$Ask her to concentrate on her own output$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage an areca plate pressing unit. A machine failure means the team will miss a bonus they were close to. It was nobody's fault. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell them where they got to and take the shortfall to the owner$qb$, $qb$Explain that the failure was outside anyone's control$qb$, $qb$Tell them the bonus will be within reach next month$qb$, $qb$Thank them for how close they came$qb$, $qb$Report the missed bonus without further comment$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a neem oil pressing unit. A long-standing customer has praised your oil in a letter addressed to you personally. The quality comes from the pressing crew. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Read the letter to the crew and tell the customer who earned it$qb$, $qb$Show the letter to the crew and thank them$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer that the crew deserves the credit$qb$, $qb$Put the letter up where the crew will see it$qb$, $qb$Thank the customer and mention it to the crew$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-GRA-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a millet flour chakki. A power cut has ruined a morning's grinding and the miller has stayed late twice this week already. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Send him home and take the evening grinding yourself$qb$, $qb$Thank him and tell him not to stay late again$qb$, $qb$Ask him whether he is able to stay again tonight$qb$, $qb$Explain that the power cuts are outside your control$qb$, $qb$Ask him to make the time up when things are quieter$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
