  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A decision recorded where the team can find it saves the same question being asked ______.$qb$, $qb$again$qb$, $qb$loudly$qb$, $qb$formally$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, $qb$publicly$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Expecting an instant reply from someone in another time zone makes them work your ______.$qb$, $qb$hours$qb$, $qb$wages$qb$, $qb$systems$qb$, $qb$premises$qb$, $qb$language$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are handing work to a colleague who starts as you finish. What matters most in the note?$qb$, $qb$What they can act on without asking you$qb$, $qb$What you have completed so far$qb$, $qb$What went wrong during your shift$qb$, $qb$How long each part took$qb$, $qb$What you would do next if you were staying$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You need an answer from someone eight hours behind you. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Send the question with everything needed to answer it$qb$, $qb$Send the question and ask them to reply as soon as they can$qb$, $qb$Send the question and follow up if there is no reply$qb$, $qb$Wait until your hours overlap and ask then$qb$, $qb$Ask someone in your own hours instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are writing to ask a colleague for something. What makes it easy for them to act?$qb$, $qb$It says what is needed and by when$qb$, $qb$It is short$qb$, $qb$It is polite$qb$, $qb$It explains the background fully$qb$, $qb$It is sent to the right person$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague sends you a long message and the request is in the last line. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Ask them to put the request first in future$qb$, $qb$Reply to the request and ignore the rest$qb$, $qb$Read it fully before replying$qb$, $qb$Ask them to summarise it for you$qb$, $qb$Reply only when you have time to read it all$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when everyone is copied into every message?$qb$, $qb$Nobody is sure who is supposed to act$qb$, $qb$People stop reading the messages$qb$, $qb$The information reaches everyone$qb$, $qb$Decisions take longer to make$qb$, $qb$The record becomes complete$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You will be away for a week and work will continue without you. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$That people can decide the things that will come up$qb$, $qb$A way of reaching you if it is serious$qb$, $qb$Everything written down somewhere$qb$, $qb$A clear picture of what you were working on$qb$, $qb$The date you are back$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A message you sent has been read the wrong way and caused offence. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what you meant and what you would write instead$qb$, $qb$Apologise for how it came across$qb$, $qb$Explain that no offence was intended$qb$, $qb$Speak to them rather than write again$qb$, $qb$Let it pass, since the meaning was clear enough$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main cost of marking routine messages as urgent?$qb$, $qb$Genuinely urgent ones stop being noticed$qb$, $qb$The sender loses credibility$qb$, $qb$People feel pressured unnecessarily$qb$, $qb$Other work is interrupted$qb$, $qb$It becomes a habit$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people in different countries need to agree something. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Put the options in writing so each can respond in their own hours$qb$, $qb$Find a time when both are working$qb$, $qb$Ask one of them to decide$qb$, $qb$Exchange messages until it is settled$qb$, $qb$Bring in a third person to decide$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most helps a long message thread stay usable?$qb$, $qb$A short summary of where things stand$qb$, $qb$Keeping replies brief$qb$, $qb$Removing people who are no longer involved$qb$, $qb$Changing the subject line as it moves on$qb$, $qb$Keeping everything in one thread$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have sent a question and had no reply for two days. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Send it again with a date you need it by$qb$, $qb$Send a reminder$qb$, $qb$Ask someone else the same question$qb$, $qb$Wait another day before chasing$qb$, $qb$Assume they have nothing to add$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main weakness of settling things in a live conversation when the team is spread out?$qb$, $qb$Those not present find out later or not at all$qb$, $qb$Nothing is written down$qb$, $qb$It is hard to find a time everyone can attend$qb$, $qb$Some people contribute less than others$qb$, $qb$It takes longer than writing would$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague replies to your messages within minutes at any hour. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Tell them when you actually need answers by$qb$, $qb$Thank them for being responsive$qb$, $qb$Ask them not to reply outside their hours$qb$, $qb$Send messages only during their hours$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since quick replies are helpful$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What should decide which channel you use for a message?$qb$, $qb$How soon it needs to be acted on$qb$, $qb$How long the message is$qb$, $qb$How formal the matter is$qb$, $qb$Which channel the person prefers$qb$, $qb$Whether a record is needed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are writing an update for people who were not at a meeting. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$What was decided and what it means for them$qb$, $qb$What was discussed$qb$, $qb$Who attended and who did not$qb$, $qb$How long the meeting took$qb$, $qb$What will be discussed next time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably reduces the number of clarifying questions a message generates?$qb$, $qb$Answering the obvious question before it is asked$qb$, $qb$Setting out the background fully$qb$, $qb$Choosing simpler words$qb$, $qb$Keeping the message short$qb$, $qb$Inviting the reader to come back with questions$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A written disagreement between two colleagues has gone back and forth six times. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Move it to a conversation and write down the outcome$qb$, $qb$Ask them to stop and involve you$qb$, $qb$Ask each of them to state their position once$qb$, $qb$Let them continue until it resolves$qb$, $qb$Decide the matter yourself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is most useful to include when passing unfinished work to someone else?$qb$, $qb$What you would do next and why$qb$, $qb$What you have done so far$qb$, $qb$How much time it has taken$qb$, $qb$Where the files are kept$qb$, $qb$Who else has been involved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You work with people whose first language is different from yours. What most helps in writing?$qb$, $qb$Short sentences and plain words$qb$, $qb$Being more formal than usual$qb$, $qb$Explaining more fully$qb$, $qb$Avoiding humour$qb$, $qb$Writing in their language where you can$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a design studio with a second office eight hours behind. You have a question that blocks your work and their day starts as yours ends. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Send everything they need, say it is blocking you, and say what you will do if there is no reply$qb$, $qb$Send the question and ask them to reply first thing$qb$, $qb$Send the question and work on something else$qb$, $qb$Wait until your hours overlap tomorrow$qb$, $qb$Decide it yourself and tell them afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You share one logbook with a research team who work different days from you. Your entry from yesterday has been queried twice. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Rewrite the entry so it answers both queries without you$qb$, $qb$Answer both queries in the logbook$qb$, $qb$Add more detail to future entries$qb$, $qb$Ask the team to call you if entries are unclear$qb$, $qb$Answer the queries when you are next in$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You edit a magazine with contributors in several places. One sends long messages with the actual request buried at the end. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask him to put the request at the top, and say why$qb$, $qb$Reply only to the request each time$qb$, $qb$Ask him to keep messages shorter$qb$, $qb$Read his messages fully when you have time$qb$, $qb$Continue, since the requests do get answered$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supply equipment and your engineers work in the field. Their reports arrive as short notes you often have to phone about. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Agree the few things every report must answer$qb$, $qb$Phone each engineer as the reports come in$qb$, $qb$Ask engineers to write at greater length$qb$, $qb$Move the reporting to phone calls instead$qb$, $qb$Continue, since the phone calls sort it out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You coordinate volunteers in several towns. Decisions get made in whichever group is talking and the others find out later. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Put decisions where everyone can see them before they are final$qb$, $qb$Send a summary of decisions to all groups$qb$, $qb$Ask groups to consult before deciding$qb$, $qb$Hold a meeting all groups can attend$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since decisions do reach everyone$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a mail-order seed business with two staff who work different hours from you. Customer queries get answered twice or not at all. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set a way of marking a query as taken before it is answered$qb$, $qb$Ask staff to check whether a query is answered$qb$, $qb$Divide queries between the three of you$qb$, $qb$Answer queries yourself and let staff pack orders$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since queries do get answered$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You oversee six branches. You sent an instruction last week and two branches have done something different. Both say the message was unclear. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Rewrite the instruction so it cannot be read two ways$qb$, $qb$Explain what you meant to the two branches$qb$, $qb$Ask branches to check with you if unclear$qb$, $qb$Follow up instructions with a call in future$qb$, $qb$Tell the two branches to follow the instruction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a plant where day and night shifts hand over in writing. A fault was noted at night and the day shift did not act on it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change the handover so anything needing action is separated out$qb$, $qb$Ask the night shift to flag faults more clearly$qb$, $qb$Ask the day shift to read the handover fully$qb$, $qb$Have the shifts overlap by ten minutes$qb$, $qb$Treat it as a one-off and remind both shifts$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an author working with an editor in another country. Your exchanges take a day each way and a chapter has gone back and forth four times. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set out every open point at once so one exchange settles them$qb$, $qb$Ask the editor to send all comments together$qb$, $qb$Arrange a call to work through the chapter$qb$, $qb$Accept the editor's changes to end the exchange$qb$, $qb$Continue, since the chapter is improving$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a survey team in the field reporting to an office. Field notes arrive with photographs and no explanation of what they show. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Agree what each photograph must be labelled with$qb$, $qb$Ask the team to explain their photographs$qb$, $qb$Phone the team about photographs you cannot read$qb$, $qb$Ask for fewer photographs and more written notes$qb$, $qb$Work out what the photographs show yourself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a school where staff work different shifts. Messages about pupils are being passed verbally and some are not reaching the right people. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Move pupil messages to a written place everyone checks$qb$, $qb$Ask staff to write down what they pass on$qb$, $qb$Set a handover meeting between shifts$qb$, $qb$Ask staff to confirm messages have been received$qb$, $qb$Continue, since most messages do get through$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a maintenance team covering several sites. Engineers report problems by message and you cannot tell which need attention today. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Agree a way of saying what happens if it waits until tomorrow$qb$, $qb$Ask engineers to mark reports as urgent or not$qb$, $qb$Phone engineers about reports that look serious$qb$, $qb$Deal with reports in the order they arrive$qb$, $qb$Ask engineers to call for anything urgent$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ACD-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a wholesaler whose buyers travel constantly. They send price queries at all hours and expect immediate answers. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell them when answers will come, and hold to it$qb$, $qb$Answer queries as quickly as you are able$qb$, $qb$Ask buyers to send queries during office hours$qb$, $qb$Set up an automatic reply about your hours$qb$, $qb$Answer whenever the queries arrive$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
